  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Response, Recovery and Resilience in the Health Sector in St. Vincent and the Grenadines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome and Description:
The overall objective of this project is to support the development of a modernized and expanded health care system with enhanced capacity and resiliency to respond to COVID-19 and other health security threats.
The proposed project consists of the following Components:
Component 1: Goods:
(a) Medical and non-medical equipment
(b) Laboratory Equipment, Consumables and Reagents
Component 2: Capacity Building:
(a) Staff training in specialized areas
Component 3: Institutional Strengthening:
(a) Human Resource for Health Planning and Execution
(b) Capacity for Epidemiological Surveillance
(c) Quality Assurance Unit
(d) Capacity for Mental Health Care Provisioning
Component 4: Infrastructural Works:
(a) Supply chain management in the health sector
(b) Capacity for the delivery of critical care services to COVID-19 and non-COVID-19 affected persons

Component 5: Other Services:
(a) Project Management and Auditing Services
(i) Consultancy Services for Project Management roles and Design and Supervision.
(ii) Auditing Services
(iii) Other Services</narrative>
  </description>
